The data set contains 30 runs; 29 are included in the results after excluding Run 17. With temperature-dependent water properties, the Reynolds number spans approximately $4.7\\times10^3$ to $5.0\\times10^4$. Figure~\\ref{fig:cd-re} shows run-wise coefficients for the retained runs. The diameter-averaged values are $C_D=1.143$ for the 25.4 mm cylinder, 1.152 for the 38.1 mm cylinder, and 1.157 for the 50.8 mm cylinder. These averages are descriptive only; they do not account for run-to-run repeatability or measurement uncertainty.
