where $\\nu$ is kinematic viscosity. For each run, water density and dynamic viscosity were evaluated at its logged temperature and atmospheric pressure using the IAPWS formulations \\cite{iapwsvisc,iapwsdensity}; kinematic viscosity was obtained as $\\nu=\\mu/\\rho$. This gives densities of approximately 998.6--999.1 kg m$^{-3}$ and kinematic viscosities of approximately $1.08$--$1.17\\times10^{-6}$ m$^2$ s$^{-1}$ over the measured temperature range. Run 17 is omitted from the reported drag statistics because of the baseline drift described above.
